\date{2026-09-05}
\title{The ordered subcube is glued from simplices}
\author{ulrikbuchholtz}
\taxon{Module}
\import{stt-macros}

\p{A crisp map that is an [equivalence on figures](ub-0032) of every simplex
shape is one on figures of every [ordered subcube](ub-000Y) (\ref{ub-003D}). This is what lets \ref{ub-0010}
trade the ordered subcube for simplices. Unlike the rest of the argument it
is about colimits rather than lifting: the ordered subcube is glued from
simplices, and mapping out of a glued shape is computed from the pieces.}

\p{The one fact about #{\flat} it uses is that equivalences on figures glue
along unions of subtypes (\ref{ub-0033}) and hence along filtrations
(\ref{ub-0034}), from [the module on figures](Modalities.Cohesion.Figures).
Everything else is combinatorics, outlined in \ref{ub-0035}.}

\agda{
open import Foundations.Universes
open import Algebra.Lattice

module Synthetic.Categories.OrderedGlueing
  {@♭ 𝓘} (@♭ Δ¹ : Type 𝓘) (@♭ I : Lattice Δ¹)
  where

open Lattice I renaming (0l to i0; 1l to i1)

open import Axioms.UF
}

\agda-imports{
\agda{
open import Foundations.Prelude

open import Modalities.Cohesion.Flat

open import Core.Arrows
open import Core.Joins
open import Core.SubtypeUnions
open import Modalities.Cohesion.Figures

open import Algebra.Lattice.Instances.Free.Inductive Δ¹ I

open import Synthetic.Cubes Δ¹ i0 i1
open import Synthetic.Simplicial Δ¹ I
open import Synthetic.Categories.SquareLifting Δ¹ I
open import Synthetic.Categories.PrismTriangulation Δ¹ I
open import Synthetic.Categories.ConvexSubcubes Δ¹ I
  using (□-coord ; cmp-at ; Everywhere ; Everywhere-is-prop)
}
}

\subtree[ub-0035]{
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Outline}

\p{Apart from [the filtration lemma](ub-0034), everything here is
combinatorics, and it is the combinatorics of
[the prism](ub-0024) run once per coordinate, in three steps.}

\ol{
\li{\strong{The prism.} A map that is an equivalence on simplex-figures is
one on #{\sum_{\Delta^m\times\Delta^1} \mathrm{Tri}^m}-figures
(\ref{ub-0037}).}
\li{\strong{One coordinate at a time.} Half-sort the cube: a chain
#{w : \Delta^k} of coordinates already arranged, and #{m} still free, with
every free coordinate comparable with every other and with the whole chain
(\ref{ub-0038}). The last free coordinate is comparable with the chain, so
it sits in one of the chain's gaps, and the choice of gap cuts the shape into
#{k+1} cells that meet consecutively in walls — the prism again, fibred over
the free part. A cell is the same shape with the coordinate moved into the
chain, a wall with it pinned to a level the chain already has, and both have
one fewer free coordinate. So induction on the free part alone, with the
chain's length quantified over, gives \ref{ub-003C}.}
\li{\strong{The empty chain.} #{\mathrm{O}(0,n)} is the ordered subcube,
which gives the theorem (\ref{ub-003D}).}
}

\p{Presenting #{\mathrm{Ord}_n} as the union of its #{n!} simplices
would need the family of cells to be closed under intersection, and two
staircases meet in a common refinement that neither of them names — so one
would have to normalise a total preorder on the coordinates, which means
sorting. The filtration does not: consecutive cells meet in a wall, which is
one of the cells, and that is \ref{ub-0034}. And carrying the ranking
as an explicit \em{chain} rather than as a relation on indices means the chain
is built by insertion (\ref{ub-0036}) and never has to be computed from
anything.}
}

\subtree[ub-0036]{
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Inserting a coordinate into a chain}

\p{A point of [the #{l}-th staircase](ub-0024) is a chain together with an
element sitting in its #{l}-th gap, which is a chain one longer. Inserting is
a recursion on #{l} and the chain at once: at the zeroth gap the element is
appended, and past it the chain's smallest coordinate is put back on top of the
insertion one gap down.}

\p{The two pinned ends make the count of gaps larger than the count of
coordinates, so a gap beyond the chain's length is the degenerate one where the
element is #{1}, and there the insertion runs off the end. The dimension of
the result records this: it is #{m+1} for a gap the chain actually has, and
#{m} beyond that, and one recursion covers both.}

\agda{
dim : ℕ → ℕ → ℕ
dim zero m = suc m
dim (suc l) zero = zero
dim (suc l) (suc n) = suc (dim l n)

ins : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (x : Δ^ m) (k : Δ¹) → Stair l (x , k) → Δ^ (dim l m)
last-ins
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (x : Δ^ m) (k : Δ¹) (t : Stair (suc l) (x , k))
  → last-Δ (ins (suc l) x k t) ＝ last-Δ x

ins zero x k t = (x :≥: k) ⦃ t ⦄
ins (suc l) · k t = ·
ins (suc zero) ((y :≥: j) ⦃ p ⦄) k t
  = (ins zero y k (t .snd) :≥: j) ⦃ t .fst ⦄
ins (suc (suc l)) ((y :≥: j) ⦃ p ⦄) k t
  = (ins (suc l) y k t :≥: j) ⦃ tr (j ≤_) (sym (last-ins l y k t)) p ⦄

last-ins l · k t = refl
last-ins zero (y :≥: j) k t = refl
last-ins (suc l) (y :≥: j) k t = refl
}

\p{Deleting is the same recursion backwards. At a gap the chain does not have
there is nothing to delete, and the element read back off is #{1}.}

\agda{
del : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} → Δ^ (dim l m) → Σ (Prism^ m) (Stair l)
last-del
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Δ^ (dim (suc l) m))
  → last-Δ (del (suc l) z .fst .fst) ＝ last-Δ z

del zero ((x :≥: k) ⦃ p ⦄) = ((x , k) , p)
del (suc l) {zero} · = ((· , i1) , (1-top , ≤-refl))
del (suc zero) {suc n} (((y :≥: k) ⦃ q ⦄ :≥: j) ⦃ p ⦄)
  = (((y :≥: j) ⦃ ≤-trans p q ⦄ , k) , (p , q))
del (suc (suc l)) {suc n} ((z :≥: j) ⦃ p ⦄)
  = ( ( (del (suc l) z .fst .fst :≥: j) ⦃ tr (j ≤_) (sym (last-del l z)) p ⦄
      , del (suc l) z .fst .snd )
    , del (suc l) z .snd )

last-del l {zero} · = refl
last-del zero {suc n} ((y :≥: k) :≥: j) = refl
last-del (suc l) {suc n} (z :≥: j) = refl
}

\p{The two are inverse. Both round trips are the same case analysis again, and
every case but one is #{\refl}: the exception is the degenerate gap, where the
element deleted is #{1} and the element inserted has to be shown to have been
#{1} already — which it is, since it is squeezed between the two pinned ends.}

\agda{
Δ-coord-· : (l : ℕ) → Δ-coord {0} · l ＝ i1
Δ-coord-· zero = refl
Δ-coord-· (suc l) = refl

stair-·-is-1 : (l : ℕ) (k : Δ¹) → Stair (suc l) (· , k) → k ＝ i1
stair-·-is-1 l k t = ≤-antisym (t .snd) (tr (_≤ k) (Δ-coord-· l) (t .fst))

del-ins-chain
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (x : Δ^ m) (k : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (x , k))
  → Δ-path (del l (ins l x k t) .fst .fst) x
del-ins-chain zero x k t = Δ-refl
del-ins-chain (suc l) · k t = ·
del-ins-chain (suc zero) (y :≥: j) k t = Δ-refl :≥: refl
del-ins-chain (suc (suc l)) (y :≥: j) k t
  = del-ins-chain (suc l) y k t :≥: refl

del-ins-elt
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (x : Δ^ m) (k : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (x , k))
  → del l (ins l x k t) .fst .snd ＝ k
del-ins-elt zero x k t = refl
del-ins-elt (suc l) · k t = sym (stair-·-is-1 l k t)
del-ins-elt (suc zero) (y :≥: j) k t = refl
del-ins-elt (suc (suc l)) (y :≥: j) k t = del-ins-elt (suc l) y k t

ins-del-chain
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Δ^ (dim l m))
  → Δ-path (ins l (del l z .fst .fst) (del l z .fst .snd) (del l z .snd)) z
ins-del-chain zero (x :≥: k) = Δ-refl
ins-del-chain (suc l) {zero} · = ·
ins-del-chain (suc zero) {suc n} ((y :≥: k) :≥: j) = Δ-refl
ins-del-chain (suc (suc l)) {suc n} (z :≥: j)
  = ins-del-chain (suc l) z :≥: refl
}
}

\subtree[ub-0037]{
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Equivalences on simplex-figures are equivalences on the triangulated prism}

\p{This is step 1 of [the outline](ub-0035), and it is
[the filtration lemma](ub-0034) at the staircases and the walls. Three things
go into it. The cells are simplices: [inserting](ub-0036) is an equivalence
#{S_l \simeq \Delta^{\dim(l,m)}}. The walls are simplices: #{W_l} pins the
extra coordinate at a level of the chain, so forgetting it is an equivalence
#{W_l \simeq \Delta^m}. And the incidence is the wall: a point of #{S_l} has
#{k \le c_l}, and #{c_l \le c_b} for #{l \le b}, so a point of
#{(S_0 \lor \cdots \lor S_b) \land S_{b+1}} has #{k \le c_b \le k}.}

\p{No region and no inner horn are needed: this is a colimit statement, not a
lifting one, and the cells being simplices is all of it.}

\agda{
stair≃ : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} → Σ (Prism^ m) (Stair l) ≃ Δ^ (dim l m)
stair≃ l
  = mk≃ (λ w → ins l (w .fst .fst) (w .fst .snd) (w .snd))
      (is-equiv←qinv
        ( del l
        , (λ w → subtype-ext (Stair-is-prop l)
                   (×-path→ ( Δ-ext (del-ins-chain l _ _ (w .snd))
                            , del-ins-elt l _ _ (w .snd))))
        , (λ z → Δ-ext (ins-del-chain l z))))

wall≃ : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {m} → Σ (Prism^ m) (Wall l) ≃ Δ^ m
wall≃ l
  = mk≃ (λ w → w .fst .fst)
      (is-equiv←qinv
        ( (λ x → ((x , Δ-level x l) , refl))
        , (λ w → subtype-ext (Wall-is-prop l) (×-path→ (refl , sym (w .snd))))
        , ~refl))
}

\p{The incidence, and the identification of the filtration's union with
[\code{Slots}](ub-0024), which is the same recursion written twice.}

\agda{
Slots-≤
  : (b : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Prism^ m) → Slots b z → z .snd ≤ Δ-coord (z .fst) b
Slots-≤ zero (x , k) t = t
Slots-≤ (suc b) (x , k)
  = *-prop-rec ≤-is-prop
      (λ u → ≤-trans (Slots-≤ b (x , k) u) (Δ-coord-mono x b))
      (λ t → t .snd)

stair→slots : (b : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Prism^ m) → Stair b z → Slots b z
stair→slots zero z t = t
stair→slots (suc b) z t = ι₂ t

slots-inc→
  : (b : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Prism^ m)
  → ∩-fam (Slots b) (Stair (suc b)) z → Wall (suc b) z
slots-inc→ b (x , k) (u , t) = ≤-antisym (Slots-≤ b (x , k) u) (t .fst)

slots-inc←
  : (b : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (z : Prism^ m)
  → Wall (suc b) z → ∩-fam (Slots b) (Stair (suc b)) z
slots-inc← b z p
  = ( stair→slots b z (Stairs←Wall b z p .fst)
    , Stairs←Wall b z p .snd )
}

\p{So the filtration runs, and its top stage is the triangulated prism.}

\agda{
module _
  {@♭ 𝓤 𝓥} {@♭ X : Type 𝓤} {@♭ Y : Type 𝓥} (@♭ f : X → Y)
  (hΔ : (@♭ k : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Δ^ k) f)
  where

  is-♭-equiv-on-slots : (@♭ m : ℕ) (@♭ b : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Σ (Prism^ m) (Slots b)) f
  is-♭-equiv-on-slots m b
    = ♭-equiv-on-filtration.is-♭-equiv-on-⋁ f (λ l → Stair l {m}) (λ l → Wall l {m})
        (λ l → Stair-is-prop l) (λ l → Wall-is-prop l)
        (λ b z → slots-inc→ b z) (λ b z → slots-inc← b z)
        (λ l → is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (stair≃ l) (hΔ (dim l m)))
        (λ l → is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (wall≃ l) (hΔ m))
        b

  is-♭-equiv-on-prism : (@♭ m : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Σ (Prism^ m) (Tri^ m)) f
  is-♭-equiv-on-prism m = is-♭-equiv-on-slots m m
}
}

\subtree[ub-0038]{
\taxon{Definition}
\title{A chain with free coordinates beside it}

\p{Step 2 of [the outline](ub-0035) needs a shape half sorted: some coordinates
already arranged into a chain, the rest still free. That is a pair
#{(w, u) : \Delta^k \times \square^m}, and the condition on it is that the free
coordinates are comparable with one another and with every coordinate of the
chain. Write #{\mathrm{O}(k,m)} for it. At #{m = 0} it is nothing, so the shape
is #{\Delta^k}; at #{k = 0} it is [the ordered subcube](ub-000Y).}

\p{The cube is re-presented so that #{\square^{m+1}} is #{\square^m \times
\Delta^1} on the nose, which [the library's cube](stt-00UU) is not at #{m=1};
the two agree (\ref{ub-003D}).}

\agda{
Cube : ℕ → Type 𝓘
Cube zero = 𝟙ᴸ
Cube (suc m) = Cube m × Δ¹

cmp-cube : ∀ {m} → Cube m → Δ¹ → Type 𝓘
cmp-cube {zero} _ _ = 𝟙ᴸ
cmp-cube {suc m} (u , i) j = cmp-cube u j × generating-fam-is-simplicial (i , j)

cmp-cube-is-prop : ∀ {m} (u : Cube m) (j : Δ¹) → is-prop (cmp-cube u j)
cmp-cube-is-prop {zero} u j = is-prop←is-single 𝟙ᴸ-is-singleton
cmp-cube-is-prop {suc m} (u , i) j
  = ×-is-prop (cmp-cube-is-prop u j) (generating-fam-is-simplicial-is-prop (i , j))

Ord-over : (k : ℕ) → ∀ {m} → Δ^ k → Cube m → Type 𝓘
Ord-over k {zero} w u = 𝟙ᴸ
Ord-over k {suc m} w (u , x)
  = (Ord-over k w u × comparable-all w x) × cmp-cube u x

Ord-over-is-prop
  : (k : ℕ) → ∀ {m} (w : Δ^ k) (u : Cube m) → is-prop (Ord-over k w u)
Ord-over-is-prop k {zero} w u = is-prop←is-single 𝟙ᴸ-is-singleton
Ord-over-is-prop k {suc m} w (u , x)
  = ×-is-prop
      (×-is-prop (Ord-over-is-prop k w u) (comparable-all-is-prop w x))
      (cmp-cube-is-prop u x)
}
}

\subtree[ub-0039]{
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Comparability with an enlarged chain}

\p{Inserting #{x} into the chain adds exactly one comparability to check, and
in the degenerate gap it adds none, because there #{x} is #{1} and everything
is below #{1}. So being comparable with the enlarged chain is being comparable
with the old one and with #{x}; and a free coordinate's whole obligation
towards the enlarged chain is its obligation towards the old one together with
its comparability with #{x}.}

\agda{
fam-swap
  : {x y : Δ¹}
  → generating-fam-is-simplicial (x , y) → generating-fam-is-simplicial (y , x)
fam-swap = *-prop-rec (generating-fam-is-simplicial-is-prop _) ι₂ ι₁

cmp-with-1
  : {x : Δ¹} → x ＝ i1 → (y : Δ¹) → generating-fam-is-simplicial (x , y)
cmp-with-1 p y = tr (λ z → generating-fam-is-simplicial (z , y)) (sym p) (ι₂ 1-top)

cmp-ins→
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {k} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (w , x)) (y : Δ¹)
  → comparable-all (ins l w x t) y
  → comparable-all w y × generating-fam-is-simplicial (x , y)
cmp-ins→ zero w x t y c = (c .snd , c .fst)
cmp-ins→ (suc l) · x t y c
  = (ttᴸ , cmp-with-1 (stair-·-is-1 l x t) y)
cmp-ins→ (suc zero) (z :≥: j) x t y c
  = ((c .fst , c .snd .snd) , c .snd .fst)
cmp-ins→ (suc (suc l)) (z :≥: j) x t y c
  = ( (c .fst , cmp-ins→ (suc l) z x t y (c .snd) .fst)
    , cmp-ins→ (suc l) z x t y (c .snd) .snd )

cmp-ins←
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {k} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (w , x)) (y : Δ¹)
  → comparable-all w y × generating-fam-is-simplicial (x , y)
  → comparable-all (ins l w x t) y
cmp-ins← zero w x t y (c , d) = (d , c)
cmp-ins← (suc l) · x t y _ = ttᴸ
cmp-ins← (suc zero) (z :≥: j) x t y (c , d) = (c .fst , (d , c .snd))
cmp-ins← (suc (suc l)) (z :≥: j) x t y (c , d)
  = (c .fst , cmp-ins← (suc l) z x t y (c .snd , d))

Ord-ins→
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {k m} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (w , x)) (u : Cube m)
  → Ord-over (dim l k) (ins l w x t) u
  → Ord-over k w u × cmp-cube u x
Ord-ins→ l {m = zero} w x t u o
  = (ttᴸ , ttᴸ)
Ord-ins→ l {m = suc m} w x t (u , z) o
  = ( ( ( Ord-ins→ l w x t u (o .fst .fst) .fst
        , cmp-ins→ l w x t z (o .fst .snd) .fst )
      , o .snd )
    , ( Ord-ins→ l w x t u (o .fst .fst) .snd
      , fam-swap (cmp-ins→ l w x t z (o .fst .snd) .snd) ) )

Ord-ins←
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {k m} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) (t : Stair l (w , x)) (u : Cube m)
  → Ord-over k w u × cmp-cube u x
  → Ord-over (dim l k) (ins l w x t) u
Ord-ins← l {m = zero} w x t u _ = ttᴸ
Ord-ins← l {m = suc m} w x t (u , z) (o , c)
  = ( ( Ord-ins← l w x t u (o .fst .fst , c .fst)
      , cmp-ins← l w x t z (o .fst .snd , fam-swap (c .snd)) )
    , o .snd )
}
}

\subtree[ub-003A]{
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The cells of the half-sorted shape}

\p{A point of #{\mathrm{O}(k,m+1)} has a last free coordinate #{x}, and #{x} is
comparable with every coordinate of the chain, so [it sits in one of the
gaps](ub-0026). Sitting in the #{l}-th gap is the cell #{E_l}: the staircase
condition on #{(w,x)} together with #{\mathrm{O}} for the enlarged chain, with
#{x} now part of it. The wall #{F_l} is the same with #{x} pinned at a level,
and there the chain does not grow.}

\p{Three small facts about chains first: an element below the chain's smallest
coordinate is comparable with all of them, so a point of any staircase is; a
family comparable with the whole chain is comparable with each of its
coordinates; and hence, on a wall, the other free coordinates are comparable
with #{x} for free — which is what makes the wall a cell of #{\mathrm{O}(k,m)}
and not of anything larger.}

\agda{
cmp-all←below
  : ∀ {k} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) → x ≤ last-Δ w → comparable-all w x
cmp-all←below · x p = ttᴸ
cmp-all←below ((z :≥: j) ⦃ q ⦄) x p
  = (ι₂ p , cmp-all←below z x (≤-trans p q))

stair→comparable-all
  : (l : ℕ) → ∀ {k} (w : Δ^ k) (x : Δ¹) → Stair l (w , x) → comparable-all w x
stair→comparable-all zero w x t = cmp-all←below w x t
stair→comparable-all (suc l) · x t = ttᴸ
stair→comparable-all (suc zero) (z :≥: j) x t
  = (ι₁ (t .fst) , cmp-all←below z x (t .snd))
stair→comparable-all (suc (suc l)) ((z :≥: j) ⦃ q ⦄) x t
  = ( ι₁ (≤-trans q (≤-trans (Δ-coord-min z l) (t .fst)))
    , stair→comparable-all (suc l) z x t )

comparable-all-at
  : ∀ {k} (w : Δ^ k) (y : Δ¹) → comparable-all w y
  → (b : ℕ) → generating-fam-is-simplicial (Δ-coord w b , y)
comparable-all-at · y c b
  = tr (λ z → generating-fam-is-simplicial (z , y)) (sym (Δ-coord-· b)) (ι₂ 1-top)
comparable-all-at (z :≥: j) y c zero = c .fst
comparable-all-at (z :≥: j) y c (suc b) = comparable-all-at z y (c .snd) b

cmp-cube-at
  : (b : ℕ) → ∀ {k m} (w : Δ^ k) (u : Cube m)
  → Ord-over k w u → cmp-cube u (Δ-coord w b)
cmp-cube-at b {m = zero} w u o = ttᴸ
cmp-cube-at b {m = suc m} w (u , z) o
  = ( cmp-cube-at b w u (o .fst .fst)
    , fam-swap (comparable-all-at w z (o .fst .snd) b) )
}

\agda{
module _ (k m : ℕ) where

  Cell : ℕ → Δ^ k × Cube (suc m) → Type 𝓘
  Cell l (w , (u , x))
    = Σ (Stair l (w , x)) (λ t → Ord-over (dim l k) (ins l w x t) u)

  Cell-is-prop : (l : ℕ) (z : Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) → is-prop (Cell l z)
  Cell-is-prop l (w , (u , x))
    = Σ-is-prop (Stair-is-prop l (w , x))
        (λ t → Ord-over-is-prop (dim l k) (ins l w x t) u)

  Wall-cell : ℕ → Δ^ k × Cube (suc m) → Type 𝓘
  Wall-cell l (w , (u , x)) = Wall l (w , x) × Ord-over k w u

  Wall-cell-is-prop
    : (l : ℕ) (z : Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) → is-prop (Wall-cell l z)
  Wall-cell-is-prop l (w , (u , x))
    = ×-is-prop (Wall-is-prop l (w , x)) (Ord-over-is-prop k w u)
}
}

\subtree[ub-003B]{
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{The cells cover, and consecutive ones meet in a wall}

\p{Both halves of the filtration's data, and neither says anything new. The
cells cover because [sorting](ub-0026) puts #{x} in some gap, and what is left
to check of #{\mathrm{O}} for the enlarged chain is \ref{ub-0039}.
Consecutive cells meet in a wall because their staircases do (\ref{ub-0037}),
and the wall carries the free coordinates' comparability
with #{x} for nothing, #{x} being a coordinate of the chain there.}

\agda{
module _ (k m : ℕ) where

  private
    Zc : Type 𝓘
    Zc = Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)

  cells→slots
    : (b : ℕ) (z : Zc)
    → ⋁fam (Cell k m) b z → Slots b (z .fst , z .snd .snd)
  cells→slots zero z c = c .fst
  cells→slots (suc b) z
    = *-prop-rec
        (Slots-is-prop (suc b) (z .fst , z .snd .snd))
        (λ c → ι₁ (cells→slots b z c))
        (λ c → ι₂ (c .fst))

  slots→cells
    : (b : ℕ) (z : Zc) → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd)
    → Slots b (z .fst , z .snd .snd) → ⋁fam (Cell k m) b z
  slots→cells zero (w , (u , x)) o t
    = (t , Ord-ins← 0 w x t u (o .fst .fst , o .snd))
  slots→cells (suc b) z@(w , (u , x)) o
    = *-prop-rec
        (⋁fam-is-prop (Cell k m) (Cell-is-prop k m) (suc b) z)
        (λ s → ι₁ (slots→cells b z o s))
        (λ t → ι₂ (t , Ord-ins← (suc b) w x t u (o .fst .fst , o .snd)))

  cover→ : (z : Zc) → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd) → ⋁fam (Cell k m) k z
  cover→ z@(w , (u , x)) o
    = slots→cells k z o (Tri←comparable-all w x (o .fst .snd))

  cover← : (b : ℕ) (z : Zc) → ⋁fam (Cell k m) b z → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd)
  cover← zero (w , (u , x)) c
    = ( ( Ord-ins→ 0 w x (c .fst) u (c .snd) .fst
        , stair→comparable-all 0 w x (c .fst) )
      , Ord-ins→ 0 w x (c .fst) u (c .snd) .snd )
  cover← (suc b) z@(w , (u , x))
    = *-prop-rec (Ord-over-is-prop k w (u , x))
        (cover← b z)
        (λ c → ( ( Ord-ins→ (suc b) w x (c .fst) u (c .snd) .fst
                 , stair→comparable-all (suc b) w x (c .fst) )
               , Ord-ins→ (suc b) w x (c .fst) u (c .snd) .snd ))
}

\agda{
module _ (k m : ℕ) where

  cell-inc→
    : (b : ℕ) (z : Δ^ k × Cube (suc m))
    → ∩-fam (⋁fam (Cell k m) b) (Cell k m (suc b)) z
    → Wall-cell k m (suc b) z
  cell-inc→ b z@(w , (u , x)) (c , d)
    = ( slots-inc→ b (w , x) (cells→slots k m b z c , d .fst)
      , Ord-ins→ (suc b) w x (d .fst) u (d .snd) .fst )

  cell-inc←
    : (b : ℕ) (z : Δ^ k × Cube (suc m))
    → Wall-cell k m (suc b) z
    → ∩-fam (⋁fam (Cell k m) b) (Cell k m (suc b)) z
  cell-inc← b z@(w , (u , x)) (p , o)
    = ( slots→cells k m b z ord (stair→slots b (w , x) (pair .fst))
      , (pair .snd , Ord-ins← (suc b) w x (pair .snd) u (o , cmp)) )
    where
      pair : Stair b (w , x) × Stair (suc b) (w , x)
      pair = Stairs←Wall b (w , x) p

      cmp : cmp-cube u x
      cmp = tr (cmp-cube u) (sym p) (cmp-cube-at b w u o)

      ord : Ord-over k w (u , x)
      ord = ((o , stair→comparable-all b w x (pair .fst)) , cmp)
}
}

\subtree[ub-003C]{
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Equivalences on simplex-figures are equivalences on the half-sorted shape}

\p{Step 2 of [the outline](ub-0035), by induction on the number of free
coordinates. With none left the shape is the chain itself, which is a simplex.
With one more, [the filtration lemma](ub-0034) applies to
[the cells and the walls](ub-003A): they cover and meet correctly
(\ref{ub-003B}), and each of them is a half-sorted shape with one fewer
free coordinate — the cell because the last free coordinate has joined the
chain (\ref{ub-0036}), the wall because it has been pinned to a level the
chain already has. The chain grows and the free part shrinks, so the induction
is on the free part alone and the chain's length is quantified over.}

\agda{
cell≃
  : (k m l : ℕ)
  → Σ (Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) (Cell k m l)
  ≃ Σ (Δ^ (dim l k) × Cube m) (λ z → Ord-over (dim l k) (z .fst) (z .snd))
cell≃ k m l = mk≃ fwd (is-equiv←qinv (bwd , ret , sec))
  where
    fwd : Σ (Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) (Cell k m l)
        → Σ (Δ^ (dim l k) × Cube m) (λ z → Ord-over (dim l k) (z .fst) (z .snd))
    fwd ((w , (u , x)) , (t , o)) = ((ins l w x t , u) , o)

    bwd : Σ (Δ^ (dim l k) × Cube m) (λ z → Ord-over (dim l k) (z .fst) (z .snd))
        → Σ (Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) (Cell k m l)
    bwd ((W , u) , o)
      = ( (del l W .fst .fst , (u , del l W .fst .snd))
        , ( del l W .snd
          , tr (λ V → Ord-over (dim l k) V u)
               (sym (Δ-ext (ins-del-chain l W))) o ) )

    ret : (z : Σ (Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) (Cell k m l)) → bwd (fwd z) ＝ z
    ret ((w , (u , x)) , (t , o))
      = subtype-ext (Cell-is-prop k m l)
          (×-path→ ( Δ-ext (del-ins-chain l w x t)
                   , ×-path→ (refl , del-ins-elt l w x t)))

    sec : (z : Σ (Δ^ (dim l k) × Cube m)
                 (λ z' → Ord-over (dim l k) (z' .fst) (z' .snd)))
        → fwd (bwd z) ＝ z
    sec ((W , u) , o)
      = subtype-ext (λ z → Ord-over-is-prop (dim l k) (z .fst) (z .snd))
          (×-path→ (Δ-ext (ins-del-chain l W) , refl))

wall-cell≃
  : (k m l : ℕ)
  → Σ (Δ^ k × Cube (suc m)) (Wall-cell k m l)
  ≃ Σ (Δ^ k × Cube m) (λ z → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd))
wall-cell≃ k m l
  = mk≃ (λ w → ((w .fst .fst , w .fst .snd .fst) , w .snd .snd))
      (is-equiv←qinv
        ( (λ z → ( (z .fst .fst , (z .fst .snd , Δ-level (z .fst .fst) l))
                 , (refl , z .snd) ))
        , (λ w → subtype-ext (Wall-cell-is-prop k m l)
                   (×-path→ (refl , ×-path→ (refl , sym (w .snd .fst)))))
        , ~refl))

base≃ : (k : ℕ) → Σ (Δ^ k × Cube 0) (λ z → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd)) ≃ Δ^ k
base≃ k
  = mk≃ (λ z → z .fst .fst)
      (is-equiv←qinv
        ( (λ w → ((w , ttᴸ) , ttᴸ))
        , (λ z → subtype-ext (λ z' → Ord-over-is-prop k (z' .fst) (z' .snd))
                   (×-path→ (refl , 𝟙ᴸ-is-singleton .central _)))
        , ~refl))
}

\agda{
module _
  {@♭ 𝓤 𝓥} {@♭ X : Type 𝓤} {@♭ Y : Type 𝓥} (@♭ f : X → Y)
  (hΔ : (@♭ k : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Δ^ k) f)
  where

  is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over
    : (@♭ m : ℕ) (@♭ k : ℕ)
    → is-♭-equiv-on (Σ (Δ^ k × Cube m) (λ z → Ord-over k (z .fst) (z .snd))) f
  is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over zero k = is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (base≃ k) (hΔ k)
  is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over (suc m) k
    = is-♭-equiv-on←iff f (λ z → Ord-over-is-prop k (z .fst) (z .snd))
        (⋁fam-is-prop (Cell k m) (Cell-is-prop k m) k)
        (cover→ k m) (cover← k m k)
        (♭-equiv-on-filtration.is-♭-equiv-on-⋁ f (Cell k m) (Wall-cell k m)
          (Cell-is-prop k m) (Wall-cell-is-prop k m)
          (cell-inc→ k m) (cell-inc← k m)
          (λ l → is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (cell≃ k m l) (is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over m (dim l k)))
          (λ l → is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (wall-cell≃ k m l) (is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over m k))
          k)
}
}

\subtree[ub-003D]{
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Equivalences on simplex-figures are equivalences on the ordered subcube}

\p{The half-sorted shape with an empty chain is [the ordered
subcube](ub-000Y), so \ref{ub-003C} at #{k = 0} says that a crisp map that
is an equivalence on #{\Delta^k}-figures for every #{k} is an equivalence on
#{\mathrm{Ord}_n}-figures for every #{n}.}

\p{Two identifications are all that is between them, and both are
bookkeeping. The cube of \ref{ub-0038} puts a #{\Delta^1} on the right at
every step, where [the library's](stt-00UU) starts at #{\square^1 = \Delta^1};
and \code{Ord-over} recurses on the coordinates where
[\code{Everywhere}](ub-002Z) quantifies over pairs of them, so the two are
matched by the same induction in both directions.}

\agda{
□←Cube : ∀ {n} → Cube n → □^ n
□←Cube {zero} u = u
□←Cube {suc zero} (u , x) = x
□←Cube {suc (suc n)} (u , x) = (□←Cube u , x)

Cube←□ : ∀ {n} → □^ n → Cube n
Cube←□ {zero} v = v
Cube←□ {suc zero} v = (ttᴸ , v)
Cube←□ {suc (suc n)} (v , x) = (Cube←□ v , x)

□-Cube-η : ∀ {n} (v : □^ n) → □←Cube (Cube←□ v) ＝ v
□-Cube-η {zero} v = refl
□-Cube-η {suc zero} v = refl
□-Cube-η {suc (suc n)} (v , x) = ×-path→ (□-Cube-η v , refl)

Cube-□-η : ∀ {n} (u : Cube n) → Cube←□ (□←Cube u) ＝ u
Cube-□-η {zero} u = refl
Cube-□-η {suc zero} (u , x)
  = ×-path→ (𝟙ᴸ-is-singleton .central u , refl)
Cube-□-η {suc (suc n)} (u , x) = ×-path→ (Cube-□-η u , refl)
}

\agda{
private
  cmp-cube→
    : ∀ {n} (u : Cube n) (t : Δ¹) → cmp-cube u t
    → (a : Fin n) → generating-fam-is-simplicial (□-coord (□←Cube u) a , t)
  cmp-cube→ {suc zero} (u , i) t c fzero = c .snd
  cmp-cube→ {suc (suc n)} (u , i) t c fzero = c .snd
  cmp-cube→ {suc (suc n)} (u , i) t c (fsuc a) = cmp-cube→ u t (c .fst) a

  cmp-cube←
    : ∀ {n} (u : Cube n) (t : Δ¹)
    → ((a : Fin n) → generating-fam-is-simplicial (□-coord (□←Cube u) a , t))
    → cmp-cube u t
  cmp-cube← {zero} u t h = ttᴸ
  cmp-cube← {suc zero} (u , i) t h = (ttᴸ , h fzero)
  cmp-cube← {suc (suc n)} (u , i) t h
    = (cmp-cube← u t (λ a → h (fsuc a)) , h fzero)

  ordC→ : ∀ {n} (u : Cube n) → Ord-over 0 · u → Everywhere (□←Cube u)
  ordC→ {suc zero} (u , x) o fzero fzero = ι₁ ≤-refl
  ordC→ {suc (suc n)} (u , x) o fzero fzero = ι₁ ≤-refl
  ordC→ {suc (suc n)} (u , x) o fzero (fsuc b)
    = fam-swap (cmp-cube→ u x (o .snd) b)
  ordC→ {suc (suc n)} (u , x) o (fsuc a) fzero = cmp-cube→ u x (o .snd) a
  ordC→ {suc (suc n)} (u , x) o (fsuc a) (fsuc b) = ordC→ u (o .fst .fst) a b

  ordC← : ∀ {n} (u : Cube n) → Everywhere (□←Cube u) → Ord-over 0 · u
  ordC← {zero} u h = ttᴸ
  ordC← {suc zero} (u , x) h = ((ttᴸ , ttᴸ) , ttᴸ)
  ordC← {suc (suc n)} (u , x) h
    = ( ( ordC← u (λ a b → h (fsuc a) (fsuc b))
        , ttᴸ )
      , cmp-cube← u x (λ a → h (fsuc a) fzero) )

ordered≃
  : (n : ℕ)
  → Σ (□^ n) (Everywhere {n})
  ≃ Σ (Δ^ 0 × Cube n) (λ z → Ord-over 0 (z .fst) (z .snd))
ordered≃ n = mk≃ fwd (is-equiv←qinv (bwd , ret , sec))
  where
    fwd : Σ (□^ n) (Everywhere {n})
        → Σ (Δ^ 0 × Cube n) (λ z → Ord-over 0 (z .fst) (z .snd))
    fwd (v , h)
      = ( (· , Cube←□ v)
        , ordC← (Cube←□ v) (tr Everywhere (sym (□-Cube-η v)) h) )

    bwd : Σ (Δ^ 0 × Cube n) (λ z → Ord-over 0 (z .fst) (z .snd))
        → Σ (□^ n) (Everywhere {n})
    bwd ((· , u) , o) = (□←Cube u , ordC→ u o)

    ret : (z : Σ (□^ n) (Everywhere {n})) → bwd (fwd z) ＝ z
    ret (v , h) = subtype-ext Everywhere-is-prop (□-Cube-η v)

    sec : (z : Σ (Δ^ 0 × Cube n) (λ z' → Ord-over 0 (z' .fst) (z' .snd)))
        → fwd (bwd z) ＝ z
    sec ((· , u) , o)
      = subtype-ext (λ z → Ord-over-is-prop 0 (z .fst) (z .snd))
          (×-path→ (refl , Cube-□-η u))
}

\agda{
module _
  {@♭ 𝓤 𝓥} {@♭ X : Type 𝓤} {@♭ Y : Type 𝓥} (@♭ f : X → Y)
  (hΔ : (@♭ k : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Δ^ k) f)
  where

  is-♭-equiv-on-ordered-subcube
    : (@♭ n : ℕ) → is-♭-equiv-on (Σ (□^ n) (Everywhere {n})) f
  is-♭-equiv-on-ordered-subcube n
    = is-♭-equiv-on←≃ f (ordered≃ n) (is-♭-equiv-on-Ord-over f hΔ n 0)
}
}
